From 06f42313718961c93f66ea6998a93772c403ac0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:19:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [games] Keep each game's saves and state in one folder

Savestates, in-game saves, disc state and cheat choices were kept in
four places under four keys, two of them only the file name, so games
with the same file name in different folders shared saves. Keep them
all in special://profile/games/<file name>_<CRC of path>/, the key disc
state already used.

In-game saves take RetroArch's names, savedata.srm and savedata.rtc, so
they can be copied between the two and no longer share .sav with
savestates. Nothing is migrated.
